WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:10.180
Jerry, squeeze my hand if you can hear me.

00:00:12.640 --> 00:00:14.640
All I know is how to be a writer...

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:23.420
There is nothing more sacred than "story."

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:25.500
How does that sound, Mr. Salinger?

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:32.000
Through the course of my fascinatingly dull life, I've always found fiction more truthful than reality.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.060
I write short stories

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.300
Have you been published?

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:36.300
You're not the first wise-ass that I've taught.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.300
I can't stand all these flits and phonies.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.460
So what do I do now?

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:42.140
You're a writer, what do you think you do now? 
Write another story?

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:44.320
And then another one after that.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:46.100
How is writing a real profession?

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:48.300
And then another one after that!

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:51.580
I don't know if I'm cut out for this.
Maybe not

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:58.300
Are you willing to devote your life to telling stories?

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:01.100
There's no harm in dumbing it down once in a while

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:04.000
You're trying to be clever on every page. It just doesn't feel real

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:08.300
What makes you think you have anything to say to people?

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.300
You can enrapture people,

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:12.580
Move people

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:14.580
I just want my writing to be truthful

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:18.269
To the best student I've ever had. Stay alive

00:01:22.890 --> 00:01:27.829
War Hero doesn't always get a parade. Sometimes he blows his head off

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:31.909
You've gotta stick out these dry spells

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.959
I think Holden Caulfield is a novel.
No I couldn't write a whole novel

00:01:36.869 --> 00:01:39.799
Holden Caulfield deserves an entire book

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:44.560
People think it has a lot of problems.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:46.780
I just don't buy Holden.
He's old and supposed to be crazy

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:49.340
They don't want to publish it

00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:51.340
I went to war with these guys over this

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:57.260
War? You went to war with these guys? I saw them all get killed. I should be dead too, I shouldn't be here

00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:00.520
The pages of this book were with me when I stormed the Beaches of Normandy

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:03.520
I don't think I'd be alive if it wasn't for this book

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:18.080
You're Holden Caulfield right?

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:23.120
Imagine the book that you would want to read and then go write it

